  ConstDecl
    LineComment "// The ternary \"?:\" is the value form of a two-way choice: cond ? a : b folds to"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// a when the condition holds and to b otherwise. Unlike if (E-9, a statement that"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// drives control flow by returning), the ternary is an expression — it yields a"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// value, so it appears wherever a value is wanted (a const initializer, a method"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// body's return). The condition must be a bool and the two branches must share a"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// type; the result is that shared type."
    Newline "\n"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// The condition is an ordinary boolean expression; the branches are values."
    Newline "\n"
